# The command that the launcher runs on the host to place AIStor's licence, on standard input of one SSH command: the host's interpreter in isolated mode and the installed
# script. The licence arrives on standard input, so sudo must not record it. These entries turn off every recording of input and output for this command and for no
# other, whatever the host's global defaults say: command defaults are parsed after global, host, user and runas defaults, and the last matching entry wins (sudoers
# manual, sudo 1.9.15 of Ubuntu 24.04). A per-command Defaults entry may not hold arguments, so the command is an alias. This file grants no privilege.
Cmnd_Alias AISTOR_LICENCE_INSTALL = /usr/bin/python3 -I /opt/platform/bin/aistor_licence_install
Defaults!AISTOR_LICENCE_INSTALL !log_input, !log_output, !log_stdin, !log_stdout, !log_stderr, !log_ttyin, !log_ttyout
